# Per-stack config (Pulumi.<stack>.yaml) holds environment-specific settings and
# encrypted secrets; the Pulumi Cloud backend is the source of truth. Only the
# project file (Pulumi.yaml) is committed.
Pulumi.*.yaml
!Pulumi.yaml
# tabula's stack configs are deliberately committed (config-as-code, like
# repo_config's Pulumi.dev.yaml): they hold only non-secret identifiers
# (project id, region, deployer SA email, adoption flags). Runtime secrets
# stay in GCP Secret Manager.
!apps/tabula/Pulumi.*.yaml
# oauth-user-inspector likewise commits its dev stack config (project id, region).
# Its deploy workflow only sets oauth-user-inspector:imageTag, so cfg.Require("project")
# must resolve from this committed file. Runtime secrets stay in GCP Secret Manager.
!apps/oauth-user-inspector/Pulumi.*.yaml
# oauth-user-inspector-deploy-identity (the GitHub Actions WIF + deploy/runtime SA
# bootstrap) likewise commits its dev stack config (project id, region) so
# cfg.Require("project") resolves on a clean checkout.
!apps/oauth-user-inspector-deploy-identity/Pulumi.*.yaml
# zitadel-apps commits its dev stack config (non-secret Zitadel org/project/app
# identifiers + redirect URIs) so the deploy workflow resolves them on a clean
# checkout. The Zitadel machine-user credential is injected from a pipeline
# secret at apply time, never committed.
!platform/zitadel-apps/Pulumi.*.yaml
# foundation/gcp-bootstrap commits its production stack config: only non-secret
# identifiers (org id, billing account id, group emails, parent folder id,
# github owner, the co-tenancy gate flag). It has no secret config keys (the
# monorepo WIF adaptation removed the github token path), so nothing sensitive
# is committed. Backend is Pulumi Cloud.
!foundation/gcp-bootstrap/Pulumi.*.yaml
# foundation/org-folders commits its stack config: only the org id (non-secret).
!foundation/org-folders/Pulumi.*.yaml
# foundation/gcp-org commits its production stack config: org id, billing
# account, bootstrap stack ref, governance groups, domains — all non-secret.
# The Pulumi project root lives at envs/shared (upstream 1-org/envs/shared layout).
!foundation/gcp-org/envs/shared/Pulumi.*.yaml
# foundation/gcp-environments commits per-environment stack configs: org id,
# billing account, org stack ref, parent folder — all non-secret. Each
# environment is its own leaf Pulumi project under envs/ (upstream
# 2-environments/envs/<env> layout) with a single `production` stack; the env
# identity is pinned in each leaf's main.go.
!foundation/gcp-environments/envs/*/Pulumi.*.yaml
# foundation/gcp-networks commits per-environment stack configs: env name,
# org id, billing account, network config, firewall rules — all non-secret.
# Each environment (development, nonproduction, production) is a separate stack.
!foundation/gcp-networks/Pulumi.*.yaml
# foundation/gcp-projects commits per-environment stack configs: env name,
# business code, billing account, env stack ref, project-type toggles — all
# non-secret. Each environment (development, nonproduction, production) is a
# separate stack. cfg.Require("env") must resolve on a clean checkout, so these
# MUST be committed (not gitignored).
!foundation/gcp-projects/Pulumi.*.yaml

# Compiled Pulumi program binary left behind by `go build .` (the binary is
# named after the module's last path element, i.e. "pulumi").
/pulumi
# Per-project program binary left behind by a stray `go build .` in the project
# dir (named after that module's last path element).
/zitadel-apps/zitadel-apps
/foundation/gcp-bootstrap/foundation-0-bootstrap
/foundation/org-folders/foundation-org-folders
/foundation/gcp-org/envs/shared/foundation-org-shared
/foundation/gcp-org/envs/shared/foundation-org
/foundation/gcp-environments/envs/development/foundation-environments-development
/foundation/gcp-environments/envs/nonproduction/foundation-environments-nonproduction
/foundation/gcp-environments/envs/production/foundation-environments-production
/foundation/gcp-networks/foundation-networks
/foundation/gcp-projects/foundation-projects

